<title>SINGAPORE: Nepal Oil Corp cancels Oct kerosene tender.</title>
<headline>Nepal Oil Corp cancels Oct kerosene tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Nepal Oil Corp (NOC) has cancelled its tender to buy 30,000 tonnes of superior kerosene for October 1-15 delivery, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender had attracted seven to eight offers with Kuwaiti-based International Petroleum Group (IPG) making the best offer at $245 per tonne, on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to India's east coast.</p>
<p>The tender closed on September 24.</p>
<p>Traders said the jet-kerosene fuel market was under pressure by abundant supplies, but they said NOC could get better offers if it decided to reissue the tender.  </p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
